{{file improvement|math at the bottom looks off}}

Illustrates [[set-mathematics|sets]]: the overlap of the two circles is the intersection $A \cap B = \{3, 4\}$, both circles together are the union, and 7 is in the universal set $U$ but in neither $A$ nor $B$.
